<section #sec:theorem-environments | Theorem Environments>

<sub-section | General Usage>

A theorem-like environment sets a statement in a numbered, labelled box. They all share one form — `<theorem | statement>`, `<lemma | …>`, `<definition | …>`, and so on — differing only in the label word. An optional `name` adds a parenthetical.

Available: `theorem`, `lemma`, `corollary`, `proposition`, `definition`, `example`, `remark`.

<code-block #code:thm-basic>
<theorem name=Pythagoras |
If <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> then the triangle is right-angled.
>

<definition |
A *prime* is a natural number greater than 1 whose only divisors are 1 and itself.
>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:thm-basic>
<theorem name=Pythagoras |
If <$ a^2 + b^2 = c^2 $> then the triangle is right-angled.
>

<definition |
A *prime* is a natural number greater than 1 whose only divisors are 1 and itself.
>
</minipage>

<sub-section | Arguments>

<table csv -numbered>
name (parenthetical suffix on the label), name=Pythagoras
Unnumbered (drop the "Theorem N." label), -numbered
Id, #thm:pythagoras
Class, .important
</table>

<sub-section | Notes>

Each kind keeps its own counter, so theorems number independently of definitions. Cross-reference any of them by id with `<ref @thm:pythagoras>`. A multi-word name needs quotes: `name="Law of cosines"`.
</section>

<section #sec:proofs | Proofs>

<sub-section | General Usage>

A `<proof>` is labelled "Proof." and is not numbered. Close it with a QED mark, `<$ \square $>`.

<code-block #code:proof-basic>
<theorem | The sum of two even integers is even.>

<proof |
Let <$ a = 2m $> and <$ b = 2n $>. Then <$ a + b = 2(m + n) $>,
which is even. <$ \square $>
>
</code-block>

<minipage #mp:proof-basic>
<theorem | The sum of two even integers is even.>

<proof |
Let <$ a = 2m $> and <$ b = 2n $>. Then <$ a + b = 2(m + n) $>,
which is even. <$ \square $>
>
</minipage>

<sub-section | Notes>

A `name` turns the label into "Proof (of Theorem 1)." for a proof set apart from its statement.
</section>
